{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1428235-naming-conventions-in-exalted","id":1428235,"title":"Naming Conventions in Exalted","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-12T22:06:06-08:00","id":1428235,"title":"Naming Conventions in Exalted","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Are there any conventions for coming up with names for your Exalt, or is it just anything goes?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12378-fma245","name":"FMA245","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-13T07:34:04-08:00","id":1428268,"title":"","content":"Take a look at the creative resources in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/65025-exalted-3rd-edition-useful-links-and-topics\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...nks-and-topics</a> - those have lots of exalted name hints.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9729-hira-akigi","name":"Hira Akigi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-13T14:36:14-08:00","id":1428303,"title":"","content":"If you mean in-setting, Realm and Prasadi names are discussed but not anywhere else's that I can recall right now.<br /> <br /> If you mean among players, I believe the rule of thumb is that anything shorter than three words on a Threshold-born character means you aren't trying hard enough. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-13T16:58:22-08:00","id":1428305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1428235-naming-conventions-in-exalted?p=1428303#post1428303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you mean in-setting, Realm and Prasadi names are discussed but not anywhere else's that I can recall right now.<br /> <br /> If you mean among players, I believe the rule of thumb is that anything shorter than three words on a Threshold-born character means you aren't trying hard enough. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://keychain.patternspider.net/archive/koc0001.html\" target=\"_blank\">Rookie numbers.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-13T22:32:03-08:00","id":1428321,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t even need to hover over that link to know where it goes. XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T06:07:12-08:00","id":1428459,"title":"","content":"Creation is suffciently large and diverse that you can justify just about any kind of name. My players' characters' names include: Whispering Steel, Torrent-Enduring Stone, Yen Shih-San, Barashii, and Amelia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T04:23:34-08:00","id":1428584,"title":"","content":"Also the Abyssal thing where they don't actually have names, just titles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T08:29:26-08:00","id":1428603,"title":"","content":"Different cultures have different conventions, so unless your PCs are all supposed to have similar origins (members of the same tribe, for instance) they can pick whatever whatever style suits them. Exalted tend to pick up deed names that are more grandiose than their birth names, and Abyssals <i>have</i> to go by baroque titles because their names are forfeit. <br /> <br /> Some basic formats are...<ul><li>Pick an earth culture that is the counterpart to your character's culture and choose an existing name from that.</li> <li>Mash together cool-sounding syllables.</li> <li>Adjective Noun (Red Hawk, Cool Breeze, Resplendent Lioness, etc).</li> <li>Verbing Noun (Falling Leaf, Leaping Trout, Reaping Wind)</li> <li>X of the Y or X of Y (Kiss of Steel, Glint of the Sun's First Ray, Grace of the Tigress)</li> <li>Short action phrase (Sings of Lost Ages, Brings the Grain, Perfects the Word)</li> <li>Trolling the herald who has to announce you at court (That Light Which Shines, Without Fear or Favour, Upon Villain and Hero, Prince and Labourer Alike, And in That Brilliance Reveals to All the Essence of Life, Giving Meaning to the Darkness, And Causing Shadows to Grow Long Upon the Ground, And in the Hearts Of Men).</li> </ul><br /> If you or your players are interested, you could build naming conventions for their cultures based on their character's names, and then use those when you introduce other characters of one of those cultures. For instance, if a PC is called Red Hawk, maybe their culture tends towards names that combine a colour and an animal, so later when you introduce a merchant from their homeland, he is called White Stoat. <br /> <br /> In one of my games there is a PC called Infinite Grace of the Flowing Water. His people are travellers who make their way by entertaining audiences with music, theatre, acrobatics, etc. He made a point that this culture tends to have names with the format <i>[Virtue or Personal Trait] of the [Element, Landmark, or Natural Phenomenon]</i>. So other members of his troupe include Majesty of the Snow-Capped Mountains, Mystery of the Moonless Forest, Patience of the Oak, Wit of the Wind, Splendour of the Sunset Vista, Wisdom of the Midnight Owl, etc. These names tend to be shorted to just the &quot;virtue&quot; bit for brevity's sake, so Infinite Grace of the Flowing Water is nicknamed Infinite Grace or just Grace, and the others are abbreviated similarly for informal purposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}